cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This repository is the reproduction package for the seminar paper listed under
  "preferred-citation". Please cite the paper for the study itself, and this software
  for the code and data.
title: "ScoutPlan: calibration-aware active sensing for energy-constrained aerial crop scouting"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction package for "Development and Evaluation of a Calibration-Aware REINFORCE
  Agent for Energy-Efficient Aerial Agricultural Surveillance" (Odusina, 2026, Miva Open
  University). Informative path planning assumes the confidence signal it consumes is
  calibrated. Deep classifiers are systematically miscalibrated and degrade further under
  distribution shift, yet no prior work quantifies how that error propagates through a
  planner into mission outcomes. The study closes the gap with a controlled instrument:
  temperature scaling divides classifier logits by a scalar before the decision link,
  which leaves accuracy provably invariant while sweeping calibration error. Across 195
  executed runs, detections per joule for a coverage baseline collapse 13.4x as the
  classifier moves from overconfident to underconfident, with accuracy held at 0.8161
  throughout. Two pre-registered hypotheses are reported as not supported and refuted
  respectively: spatial clustering does not predict planner advantage, and degradation is
  not monotone in calibration error magnitude. The direction of miscalibration governs
  outcomes, not its size. All results come from a NumPy-only simulation runnable on a
  free-tier kernel.
authors:
  - family-names: Odusina
    given-names: Oluwasegun Ibrahim
    orcid: ""
